WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.735
Stage six: race day, segment by segment.

2
00:00:05.585 --> 00:00:09.206
Drop in the GPX file for the Trail des Crêtes.

3
00:00:09.306 --> 00:00:16.873
The skill measures real distance and smoothed elevation, finds the climbs, and tells loop from point-to-point.

4
00:00:17.723 --> 00:00:23.797
Next, Camille's personal curve: the pace actually held on each grade in past sessions.

5
00:00:23.897 --> 00:00:29.032
Where history is thin, the generic model steps in. And the plan says so.

6
00:00:29.882 --> 00:00:35.124
The course is cut into segments of similar grade, each timed from that curve.

7
00:00:35.224 --> 00:00:41.682
Three scenarios: safe, six forty. Realistic, six oh five. Ambitious, five thirty-eight.

8
00:00:41.782 --> 00:00:48.517
Aid stations at kilometers twelve, twenty-four, thirty-four, plus OpenStreetMap water points.

9
00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:55.057
Each section gets a planned energy cost, in kilocalories per hour, pack included.

10
00:00:55.157 --> 00:01:00.164
Next to it, sixty grams of carbs per hour: the gap is flagged, never hidden.

11
00:01:01.014 --> 00:01:07.963
Mandatory gear is checked against your inventory: missing, never used in training, or flagged for wear.

12
00:01:08.063 --> 00:01:10.318
Nothing new on race day.

13
00:01:11.168 --> 00:01:14.362
The course and aid stations go to the watch.

14
00:01:14.462 --> 00:01:21.069
And the /race command gives the countdown: minus fifty-four days, with the Trail Shape score.

15
00:01:21.919 --> 00:01:27.502
The day after, the debrief compares plan and actual race, segment by segment.

16
00:01:27.602 --> 00:01:31.436
Pace gap, late-race fade, carbs per hour taken.

17
00:01:33.986 --> 00:01:38.737
To go further: the “Course strategist” page of the documentation.
